 "text": "Hey! How are you feeling? You can still do it, though it gets trickier. Do you have a headlamp? Use the softest ones to start, like spinach leaves or carrot tops. They disappear quickly and keep the tent smelling fresh. Pack them loose, not compactly, so they don't tangle up. If it' really windy, pitch a small tarp inside to catch the water. Show him the tent when you' done. He might change his mind when he smells it. Try it while he cooking. A nice cup of herbal tea while you do it is the ultimate backcountry treat.",
